<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady on poor arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady on poor arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Thursday, with most markets closed to mark a traditional Hindu holiday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were poor as farmers held back their stocks in hopes of better prices. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on limited supplies from plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent rose by 200 rupees per tonne and soyoil refined rose by 100 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Business volumes were dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices remained steady and quoted at $270-271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction prices were slightly down and quoted at $126-127 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,350 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,300-4,325 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
